#!/usr/bin/python3
"""Screenshot: take a picture of the whole screen or of an area of it, or
record a video of it.

Every screenshot is saved into ~/Pictures/Screenshots (the folder of
`xdg-user-dir PICTURES`, where FlickOS's Print keys have always saved,
unless the folder setting says otherwise) and
copied to the clipboard as a PNG, and a notification says so; clicking it
opens the picture in the markup window. Nothing is overwritten: a second
shot in the same second gets " (2)". The shutter sound plays and what was
taken flashes white, unless
the desktop's event sounds or animations are off (GSettings
org.gnome.desktop.sound event-sounds, org.gnome.desktop.interface
enable-animations) or, for the sound, Do Not Disturb is on. Design:
docs/design/flickos-screenshot.md.

An area is chosen on a frozen screen: every screen is grabbed first (grim, as
PPM because it is quick), before GTK is even imported, and the area is drawn
on that picture, so an open menu or a tooltip stays in the shot. The area is
then cut out of the grab; nothing is grabbed twice. On the frozen screen:
drag to select an area, or click to take the whole screen under the pointer.
From the keyboard: the arrow keys move a crosshair (with Shift 10 pixels at a
time), Space marks the first corner, Enter takes the area (or, with no corner
marked, the screen under the crosshair), Tab jumps to the next screen and
Escape cancels.

The capture bar (Super+Shift+S, and Screenshot in the menus) offers Area and
Full Screen, Photo or Video (or Text, while tesseract is installed), a delay
of 3, 5 or 10 seconds and, for a video, the sound; it hides before the delay,
so nothing of it is in the picture. With
a delay an area is chosen first and taken when the delay is over, so a menu
opened meanwhile is in it. The delay it used last is remembered in
$XDG_STATE_HOME/flickos/screenshot/last. The sound, where pictures and
recordings are saved, and whether a screenshot includes the pointer are
settings (`get`/`set`; the system file /etc/xdg/flickos/screenshot.conf, then
~/.config/flickos/screenshot). flickos-settings' Print keys run `shot`
directly; Super+Shift+R opens the bar with Video chosen, or stops the
recording.

Text (`shot --text`, the bar's Text) reads the area or the screen with
tesseract (tesseract-ocr is only suggested: without it Text isn't offered),
in English and up to two more installed languages, copies the text and
prints it; the notification shows how it starts. The picture isn't saved.

The markup window (`edit`) draws on a picture with a pen, a highlighter,
arrows, boxes, text and solid boxes that hide what is under them and crops it.
It copies the result, saves it into its own file (or, for one that was only
copied, a new one) or, while flickos-phone runs, sends it to the phone. Undo
and redo go back to the picture as it was opened; the file is written only by
Save. Closing it with markup that was neither saved nor copied asks first. One
per session: another `edit` shows its picture in the open window
(edit-request, then SIGUSR1 to the PID in edit.lock).

A recording asks xdg-desktop-portal for the screen (ScreenCast) and encodes
it with GStreamer in this process, which loads no GTK: H.264 and Opus in a
fragmented MP4, so a crash keeps all but the last second. It is written
straight into ~/Videos/Screen Recordings under its final name. The panel's
recording button (custom/recording, flickos-layouts) counts down, then shows
the time and stops it when clicked: the recorder writes panel.json and sends
waybar SIGRTMIN+PANEL_SIGNAL. The area is chosen by a short-lived child (the
`area` command, the frozen screen), and another one (`outline`) draws a line
around it, outside what is recorded. FlickOS's portal-wlr config runs
/usr/libexec/flickos/screencast-chooser, which answers the portal's question
"which screen?" from screencast-request, written just before; for anyone
else's request it asks, as before. portal-wlr sometimes sends one broken frame
and then nothing: the pipeline is restarted on the same stream (Recorder).

It runs nothing in the background: every command but `record` and `edit`
ends when its picture is taken, `record` ends with the recording and `edit`
when its window is closed. The notification is
shown by a short-lived child (the `notify` command) that waits for a click,
and the sound and the flash by another one (`feedback`), started before the
grab so that it is ready when the picture is; it holds flash.lock while the
flash is shown, so the next grab waits for it. Session files are in
$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/flickos/screenshot/ (the grab while choosing an area,
last.png, the latest picture that was only copied, so its notification can
still open it, while recording recording.lock with the recorder's PID and
panel.json, and while the markup window is open edit.lock). One capture at
a time (screenshot.lock in $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/flickos), and one recording.

Commands:
  (none), bar [--video|--photo]
                     the capture bar; --video chooses Video, or stops the
                     recording that is running; --photo offers only Photo
                     and prints the picture's path (the markup window's New
                     Screenshot)
  shot region|screen [--delay N] [--copy-only|--text] [--pointer]
                     take a picture of an area (chosen on the frozen screen)
                     or of every screen, N seconds later (an area is chosen
                     first); --copy-only copies it without saving; --text
                     copies and prints the text in it instead (tesseract);
                     --pointer includes the mouse pointer
  record region|screen [--delay N] [--sound none|computer|microphone|both]
                     record an area or a screen (with several, the portal
                     asks which) after a countdown of N seconds (default 3),
                     until `stop`
  stop               stop the recording
  edit FILE          the markup window with the picture FILE
  status [--panel]   whether a recording runs; --panel: the panel button's JSON
  area               (internal) choose an area on the frozen screen, print it
  outline X Y W H    (internal) draw a line around an area until killed
  notify FILE TITLE BODY [--icon NAME] [--edit]
                     (internal) show a notification about FILE and open FILE
                     (with --edit in the markup window) when it is clicked
  feedback           (internal) once "flash [X Y W H]" comes on stdin, play the
                     shutter sound and flash the area, or every screen
  get KEY            print a setting: folder, recordings-folder, pointer, sound
  set KEY VALUE      change one ("default" puts the system's back); a change
                     is recorded for Settings > History
  state              every setting as JSON, for Settings > Screenshots

Exit codes: 0 ok, 1 error or cancelled, 2 usage error.
"""

